xnu 0259: wake the panel with the power key, not home

A home press is delivered to backboardd (one client) and changes nothing on a
panel that went to sleep, which is what the frozen display links look like from
userland. The side button is the event that wakes a sleeping display on this
userland, so the mondrianwake= presses send kHIDUsage_Csmr_Power and the log
says so. If the display is awake the same press sleeps it, so an alternating
pattern of frames every N seconds is the expected result and still answers the
question.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
@@ -449,9 +449,9 @@
 	MondrianHIDButtons *self = (MondrianHIDButtons *)owner;
 	bool press = (self->fWakeCount & 1) == 0;
 
-	self->key(kHIDUsage_Csmr_Menu, press);
+	self->key(kHIDUsage_Csmr_Power, press);
 	if (press) {
-		IOLog("MONDRIAN HID: wake %u\n", self->fWakeCount / 2);
+		IOLog("MONDRIAN HID: wake %u (power)\n", self->fWakeCount / 2);
 	}
 	self->fWakeCount++;
 	sender->setTimeoutMS(press ? 100 : self->fWakeSecs * 1000);
